<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What QuickFIX/n's FIXT11.xml and FIX50SP2.xml, read as one, place differently from the FIX 5.0 SP2
  repository (2010 edition), said the way the repository says it, in that file's format. Read after
  them: FixDictionary.Parse(FIXT11).Merge(FixDictionary.Parse(FIX50SP2)).Merge(this).

  One component. Their UsernameGrp is the field Username alone; the repository's is the repeating group
  NoUsernames (809), whose entries each hold a Username (553), and their file does not declare 809 at all.

  Two message types of theirs are of a later edition than the repository and have no class in the
  model, PartyDetailsListRequest (CF) and PartyDetailsListReport (CG). A file read over another can
  replace what it describes but not remove it, so they are removed in code (Fix50Tests).
-->
<fix>
  <components>
    <component name="UsernameGrp">
      <group name="NoUsernames" required="N">
        <field name="Username" required="N" />
      </group>
    </component>
  </components>
</fix>
